; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Hash Table Buckets
; CATEGORY: Lists & Data Structures
; LEVEL:    Advanced
; TAGS:     hash table, arrays, ascii, buckets, collisions
; SUMMARY:  Builds a hash table from an array of buckets, shows where each word lands and draws the chains that form when words collide.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   A hash function turns a word into a number. Using that number as
;   an array index lets us jump straight to the right bucket instead
;   of searching a long list. Sometimes two words land in the same
;   bucket, a collision, so each bucket holds a short list of
;   [key value] pairs. The turtle draws the array down the left and
;   the chain of pairs in each bucket to the right.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Try a different number of buckets in NBUCKETS, or the
;   simpler hash SIMPLEHASH, and see how the chains change.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * ASCII turns a character into a number
;   * a hash function mixes those numbers with MODULO
;   * an ARRAY of lists, one list per bucket
;   * collisions and why a good hash spreads words out evenly
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Use SIMPLEHASH in HASHPUT and HASHGET and compare the picture.
;   * Count the longest chain, and grow the table when it gets long.
; ============================================================

make "nbuckets 11
make "table array :nbuckets

; Adding up the letter codes is simple, but "act" and "cat" then land
; in the same bucket because the order of letters is lost.
to simplehash :w
  output 1 + modulo reduce "sum map [ascii ?] :w :nbuckets
end

; Multiplying by 31 before adding each letter makes the order matter.
; MODULO at every step keeps the number small.
to hash :w
  localmake "h 0
  foreach lowercase :w [make "h modulo :h * 31 + ascii ? 1000003]
  output 1 + modulo :h :nbuckets
end

to clearbuckets
  for [i 1 :nbuckets] [setitem :i :table []]
end

; Replace an old pair with the same key, or add a new pair.
to hashput :key :value
  localmake "b hash :key
  localmake "chain filter [not equalp first ? :key] item :b :table
  setitem :b :table fput (list :key :value) :chain
end

to hashget :key
  localmake "pair find [equalp first ? :key] item hash :key :table
  if emptyp :pair [output [not found]]
  output last :pair
end

to drawtable
  for [i 1 :nbuckets] [
    localmake "y 250 - 45 * (:i - 1)
    penup setxy -380 :y setheading 90 setpencolor "blue pendown
    repeat 2 [fd 40 rt 90 fd 30 rt 90]
    penup setxy -370 :y - 21 setpencolor "black label :i
    localmake "x -320
    foreach item :i :table [
      penup setxy :x - 20 :y - 15 setpencolor "grey pendown setxy :x :y - 15
      penup setxy :x :y setpencolor "forest pendown
      repeat 2 [fd 110 rt 90 fd 30 rt 90]
      penup setxy :x + 6 :y - 21 setpencolor "black
      label (word first ? "= last ?)
      make "x :x + 130
    ]
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
clearbuckets
foreach [[cat 4] [act 9] [dog 2] [owl 7] [eel 1] [bee 3] [ant 5] ~
         [fox 6] [yak 8] [emu 2] [hen 5] [gnu 4] [elk 1] [bat 2]] ~
        [hashput first ? last ?]
hashput "cat 10
foreach [cat act gnu bat cow] [print (sentence ? [is in bucket] hash ? [and has value] hashget ?)]
drawtable
